{
  "id": "python_py_fastapi_deployment",
  "title": "Deploying and running an API",
  "difficulty": "hard",
  "testId": "python_test_py_fastapi_deployment_en",
  "estimatedMinutes": 20,
  "sources": [
    "https://fastapi.tiangolo.com/deployment/",
    "https://www.uvicorn.org/deployment/"
  ],
  "spans": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "WHY USE THIS?\n",
      "size": 20,
      "color": "#1565C0",
      "bold": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "FastAPI builds JSON APIs that web and mobile applications call over HTTP; type annotations help validate inputs and describe the API contract.\n\n",
      "size": 16,
      "color": "#212121"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "PURPOSE AND REAL-WORLD USE\n",
      "size": 20,
      "color": "#6A1B9A",
      "bold": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "A local development server is not a production deployment. Uvicorn can serve an ASGI app, but real deployments also need environment configuration, secrets, TLS termination, health checks, logs, and restart policy. ",
      "size": 17,
      "color": "#212121"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "--reload",
      "size": 17,
      "color": "#1565C0",
      "bold": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " is for development only.\n\n",
      "size": 17,
      "color": "#212121"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "To run these examples locally, install ",
      "size": 16,
      "color": "#212121"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "pip install fastapi uvicorn httpx",
      "size": 16,
      "color": "#1565C0",
      "bold": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " plus any extra package named in the lesson. Save the server example as ",
      "size": 16,
      "color": "#212121"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "app.py",
      "size": 16,
      "color": "#1565C0",
      "bold": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " and start ",
      "size": 16,
      "color": "#212121"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "uvicorn app:app --reload",
      "size": 16,
      "color": "#1565C0",
      "bold": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": ". ",
      "size": 16,
      "color": "#212121"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "--reload",
      "size": 16,
      "color": "#1565C0",
      "bold": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " is for development only.\n\n",
      "size": 16,
      "color": "#212121"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "WHERE DOES THIS APPEAR IN REAL LIFE?\nClient apps and monitoring systems call a readiness endpoint to check service health.\n\n",
      "size": 16,
      "color": "#212121"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "If this part is omitted: Without health checks, traffic may reach a failed server; secrets committed in code can leak with the repository.\n\n",
      "size": 16,
      "color": "#212121"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "COMPLETE RUNNABLE EXAMPLE\n",
      "size": 20,
      "color": "#1565C0",
      "bold": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "QUESTION: What will this code print? Predict first, then run it.\n",
      "size": 16,
      "bold": true
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "python",
      "code": "from fastapi import FastAPI\n\napp = FastAPI()\n\n@app.get(\"/health\")\nasync def health():\n    return {\"status\": \"ready\"}\n",
      "showCopyButton": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "REQUEST AND EXPECTED RESPONSE\n",
      "size": 18,
      "color": "#2E7D32",
      "bold": true
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "text",
      "code": "Request: Uvicorn process starts app; GET /health returns readiness status\nResponse: The server listens on 127.0.0.1:8000; `/health` returns 200 JSON. The hosting platform must monitor the process.",
      "showCopyButton": false
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "LINE-BY-LINE CODE EXPLANATION\n",
      "size": 15,
      "color": "#37474F"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "from fastapi import FastAPI",
      "size": 15,
      "color": "#1565C0",
      "bold": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " — Imports FastAPI so the program can create its application object; without it, ",
      "size": 15,
      "color": "#37474F"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "FastAPI",
      "size": 15,
      "color": "#1565C0",
      "bold": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " is undefined.\n",
      "size": 15,
      "color": "#37474F"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "app = FastAPI()",
      "size": 15,
      "color": "#1565C0",
      "bold": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " — ",
      "size": 15,
      "color": "#37474F"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "FastAPI()",
      "size": 15,
      "color": "#1565C0",
      "bold": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " creates the ASGI application that holds the routes and is passed to the server.\n",
      "size": 15,
      "color": "#37474F"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "@app.get(\"/health\")",
      "size": 15,
      "color": "#1565C0",
      "bold": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " — Binds an HTTP method and URL path to this function; without the decorator, it is not an API endpoint.\n",
      "size": 15,
      "color": "#37474F"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "async def health():",
      "size": 15,
      "color": "#1565C0",
      "bold": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " — Defines the endpoint the server calls; parameter names help bind path, query, or body data.\n",
      "size": 15,
      "color": "#37474F"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "return {\"status\": \"ready\"}",
      "size": 15,
      "color": "#1565C0",
      "bold": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " — Returns the HTTP response value; FastAPI converts it to JSON and applies the response model.\n\n",
      "size": 15,
      "color": "#37474F"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "PRACTICE: CHECK IT WITH AN HTTP CLIENT\n",
      "size": 19,
      "color": "#1565C0",
      "bold": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "This complete file calls the app locally with TestClient; it does not open a server port. Install ",
      "size": 16,
      "color": "#212121"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "httpx",
      "size": 16,
      "color": "#1565C0",
      "bold": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " for TestClient.\n\n",
      "size": 16,
      "color": "#212121"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "COMPLETE RUNNABLE CLIENT TEST\n",
      "size": 20,
      "color": "#1565C0",
      "bold": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "QUESTION: What will this code print? Predict first, then run it.\n",
      "size": 16,
      "bold": true
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "python",
      "code": "from fastapi import FastAPI\n\napp = FastAPI()\n\n@app.get(\"/health\")\nasync def health():\n    return {\"status\": \"ready\"}\n\nfrom fastapi.testclient import TestClient\n\nwith TestClient(app) as client:\n    response = client.get(\"/health\")\n    print(response.status_code, response.json())\n",
      "showCopyButton": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "EXPECTED CLIENT-TEST OUTPUT\n",
      "size": 18,
      "color": "#2E7D32",
      "bold": true
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "text",
      "code": "200 {'status': 'ready'}",
      "showCopyButton": false
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "LINE-BY-LINE CODE EXPLANATION\n",
      "size": 15,
      "color": "#37474F"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "from fastapi import FastAPI",
      "size": 15,
      "color": "#1565C0",
      "bold": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " — Imports FastAPI so the program can create its application object; without it, ",
      "size": 15,
      "color": "#37474F"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "FastAPI",
      "size": 15,
      "color": "#1565C0",
      "bold": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " is undefined.\n",
      "size": 15,
      "color": "#37474F"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "app = FastAPI()",
      "size": 15,
      "color": "#1565C0",
      "bold": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " — ",
      "size": 15,
      "color": "#37474F"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "FastAPI()",
      "size": 15,
      "color": "#1565C0",
      "bold": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " creates the ASGI application that holds the routes and is passed to the server.\n",
      "size": 15,
      "color": "#37474F"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "@app.get(\"/health\")",
      "size": 15,
      "color": "#1565C0",
      "bold": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " — Binds an HTTP method and URL path to this function; without the decorator, it is not an API endpoint.\n",
      "size": 15,
      "color": "#37474F"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "async def health():",
      "size": 15,
      "color": "#1565C0",
      "bold": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " — Defines the endpoint the server calls; parameter names help bind path, query, or body data.\n",
      "size": 15,
      "color": "#37474F"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "return {\"status\": \"ready\"}",
      "size": 15,
      "color": "#1565C0",
      "bold": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " — Returns the HTTP response value; FastAPI converts it to JSON and applies the response model.\n",
      "size": 15,
      "color": "#37474F"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "from fastapi.testclient import TestClient",
      "size": 15,
      "color": "#1565C0",
      "bold": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " — Imports TestClient so an HTTP request can exercise the app without opening a server port.\n",
      "size": 15,
      "color": "#37474F"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "with TestClient(app) as client:",
      "size": 15,
      "color": "#1565C0",
      "bold": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " — Creates a test HTTP client for the app and closes it when the context ends.\n",
      "size": 15,
      "color": "#37474F"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "response = client.get(\"/health\")",
      "size": 15,
      "color": "#1565C0",
      "bold": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " — Sends the stated GET request through the test client and stores the response.\n",
      "size": 15,
      "color": "#37474F"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "print(response.status_code, response.json())",
      "size": 15,
      "color": "#1565C0",
      "bold": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " — Reads and prints both the HTTP status code and parsed JSON response.\n\n",
      "size": 15,
      "color": "#37474F"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "COMMON MISTAKES\n",
      "size": 20,
      "color": "#C62828",
      "bold": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Using ",
      "size": 16,
      "color": "#212121"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "--reload",
      "size": 16,
      "color": "#1565C0",
      "bold": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": ", exposing debug details, or hardcoding secrets in production; use external environment configuration.\n\n",
      "size": 16,
      "color": "#212121"
    },
    {
      "type": "tip",
      "title": "Practical tip",
      "text": "Start with `uvicorn app:app --host 127.0.0.1 --port 8000`, then adapt process and health checks to your hosting platform."
    },
    {
      "type": "detail",
      "title": "One level deeper",
      "text": "A process manager or container handles restarts and monitoring; choose worker count and state storage for the deployment model."
    },
    {
      "type": "warning",
      "title": "Important warning",
      "text": "Host, firewall, proxy, secret manager, resource limits, and migrations are platform-specific; this is not a turnkey production configuration."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "QUICK RECALL\n",
      "size": 20,
